1
00:00:01,583 --> 00:00:03,041
What is radiation?

2
00:00:03,041 --> 00:00:05,750
Why is it important?

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,708
Radiation treatment
can be thought of as high energy rays,

4
00:00:09,708 --> 00:00:13,208
like powerful
x-rays that are directed at the tumors

5
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:16,208
to stop the cells
from growing and dividing.

6
00:00:16,666 --> 00:00:21,500
This video series focuses
specifically on external beam radiation,

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,625
in which the radiation is delivered
from an energy source

8
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:28,375
outside the body through a beam of energy.

9
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:33,208
No radiation is implanted within the body,
but you may hear of another

10
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:37,041
type of radiation called brachytherapy,
which is internal.

11
00:00:37,041 --> 00:00:39,833
That will not be discussed here.

12
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:43,208
Radiation works
because these X-ray beams cause breaks

13
00:00:43,208 --> 00:00:48,250
in the DNA of the cancer cells,
which prevents them from surviving.

14
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:52,791
This is also how radiation targets
the cancer cells

15
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:55,333
while sparing your healthy cells.

16
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,625
Your healthy cells

17
00:00:56,625 --> 00:01:00,708
have the cellular machinery
within them to repair these DNA breaks

18
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:04,791
so the healthy cells can survive
while the cancer cells, due

19
00:01:04,791 --> 00:01:09,666
to their abnormal growth, do not have
the tools necessary to repair the DNA.
